::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Independent learning does not mean working without support. Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. What is the central claim? {
~A. Independent learning requires avoiding support.#This contradicts the passage.
=B. Independent learning combines responsibility with thoughtful use of support.#Correct. This captures the central claim.
~C. Feedback automatically improves work.#This is too broad.
~D. Revision is unnecessary for independent learners.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. What does revise mean? {
~A. Ignore#This is the opposite.
=B. Review and improve#Correct. Revise means review and improve.
~C. Copy without thought#This is not revision.
~D. Finish without checking#This is not revision.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A student who receives feedback but does not examine it carefully may repeat the same error, while a student who studies the feedback can identify the pattern behind the mistake. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
=A. Feedback helps most when students study it closely enough to recognize patterns in their mistakes.#Correct. This preserves the contrast.
~B. Feedback always improves work automatically.#This ignores the condition.
~C. Students should avoid feedback because it causes errors.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Studying feedback makes students repeat the same error.#This reverses the meaning.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which sentence is punctuated correctly? {
~A. Learners use resources, deliberately ask focused questions evaluate feedback and revise their work.#The punctuation blurs the series.
=B. Learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work.#Correct. The series is clear.
~C. Learners use resources deliberately ask, focused questions, evaluate feedback and revise their work.#The comma is misplaced.
~D. Learners, use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work.#The first comma incorrectly separates subject and verb.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: Strong independent learning therefore depends on both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of available support. Which oral explanation is most coherent? {
~A. Independent learning is support and responsibility and stuff.#This is vague.
=B. The passage argues that independent learners must take responsibility while also using support thoughtfully.#Correct. This is coherent and accurate.
~C. Support is bad because independent means alone.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Responsibility means never asking questions.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q06::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. What does focused mean? {
=A. Specific and directed#Correct. Focused questions are specific.
~B. Random#This is the opposite.
~C. Decorative#This is unrelated.
~D. Avoided#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q07::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Independent learning does not mean working without support. Which paraphrase distorts the source? {
~A. Independent learning can include support.#This is accurate.
=B. Independent learning means refusing support.#Correct. This contradicts the source.
~C. Independent learning is not the same as isolation.#This is accurate.
~D. Independent learners may ask focused questions.#This is accurate.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q08::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: A student who studies the feedback can identify the pattern behind the mistake. Which sentence follows standard conventions? {
~A. A student who study feedback can identify patterns.#Subject-verb agreement is incorrect.
=B. A student who studies feedback can identify patterns.#Correct. Subject and verb agree.
~C. A student who studies feedback can identifies patterns.#The verb form is incorrect.
~D. a student who studies feedback can identify patterns.#The sentence begins with a lowercase letter.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q09::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: In college and workplace settings, this habit matters because people are expected to improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection. Which claim is supported? {
~A. Evidence and feedback are unnecessary outside school.#This contradicts the passage.
=B. The habit of improving from feedback supports college and workplace readiness.#Correct. This follows the final sentence.
~C. Reflection prevents people from improving.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. People are never expected to improve work.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q10::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: In college and workplace settings, this habit matters because people are expected to improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection. What does reflection mean here? {
~A. Light bouncing from a surface#This is the wrong context.
=B. Careful thought about work and improvement#Correct. Reflection means thoughtful review.
~C. A spelling rule#This is unrelated.
~D. A public speech#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q11::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which presentation order is strongest? {
~A. Random example, unrelated opinion, claim#This lacks organization.
=B. Claim, paraphrased evidence, rationale, conclusion#Correct. This is coherent.
~C. Vocabulary only, no claim#This is incomplete.
~D. Conclusion first, no evidence#This is weak.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q12::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A student who receives feedback but does not examine it carefully may repeat the same error. What is the function of this detail? {
~A. It proves feedback is useless.#This overstates the detail.
=B. It shows why students must evaluate feedback instead of only receiving it.#Correct. It supports the passage's claim.
~C. It says students should ignore mistakes.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. It introduces an unrelated example.#It is directly related.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q13::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Strong independent learning therefore depends on both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of available support. Which sentence is clear and conventional? {
=A. Strong independent learning depends on responsibility and thoughtful use of support.#Correct. This is clear and conventional.
~B. Strong independent learning depend on responsibility and support.#Subject-verb agreement is incorrect.
~C. Strong independent learning, depends on responsibility and support.#The comma separates subject and verb.
~D. strong independent learning depends on responsibility and support.#The sentence begins with a lowercase letter.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q14::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Strong independent learning therefore depends on both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of available support. What does depends on mean? {
~A. Rejects#This is the opposite.
=B. Relies on#Correct. Depends on means relies on.
~C. Decorates#This is unrelated.
~D. Copies#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q15::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which paraphrase is most complete? {
~A. Independent learners use resources.#This is too incomplete.
=B. Effective independent learners intentionally use resources, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise.#Correct. This preserves the full list.
~C. Independent learners only revise work.#This is too narrow.
~D. Independent learners avoid resources and questions.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q16::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: In college and workplace settings, this habit matters because people are expected to improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection. Which oral explanation uses academic vocabulary effectively? {
~A. This habit is good because work stuff matters.#This is vague.
=B. This habit supports readiness because college and workplace audiences expect improvement through evidence, feedback, and reflection.#Correct. This is precise and coherent.
~C. This habit is obviously perfect everywhere.#This overstates the claim.
~D. Evidence is feedback and reflection is evidence.#This confuses terms.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q17::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: In college and workplace settings, this habit matters because people are expected to improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection. Which sentence punctuates the series correctly? {
~A. People improve work from evidence feedback and reflection.#Commas are missing.
=B. People improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection.#Correct. The series is clear.
~C. People improve work, from evidence feedback, and reflection.#The commas are misplaced.
~D. People, improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection.#The first comma is incorrect.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q18::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Independent learning does not mean working without support. Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which answer best combines both sentences? {
=A. Independent learning includes responsible use of support such as resources, questions, feedback, and revision.#Correct. This synthesizes both sentences.
~B. Independent learning means never using resources.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. Effective learners only ask questions but never revise.#This is incomplete and inaccurate.
~D. Support prevents independent learning.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q19::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A student who studies the feedback can identify the pattern behind the mistake. What does pattern mean here? {
~A. A decorative design#This is the wrong context.
=B. A repeated form or recurring issue#Correct. A pattern is a repeated issue.
~C. A complete sentence#This is unrelated.
~D. A public audience#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q20::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: Strong independent learning therefore depends on both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of available support. Which phrase should be emphasized in an oral explanation? {
~A. Only personal responsibility#This omits support.
~B. Only available support#This omits responsibility.
=C. Both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of support#Correct. This preserves the balanced claim.
~D. Neither support nor responsibility#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q21::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A student who receives feedback but does not examine it carefully may repeat the same error, while a student who studies the feedback can identify the pattern behind the mistake. What relationship is shown? {
~A. Chronology only#The sentence is not mainly time order.
=B. Contrast#Correct. It contrasts two ways of responding to feedback.
~C. Definition of college#This is not a definition.
~D. Unrelated examples#The examples are related.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q22::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which revision fixes the error? Original: Effective independent learners uses resources deliberately. {
~A. Effective independent learners uses resources deliberately.#The error remains.
=B. Effective independent learners use resources deliberately.#Correct. The plural subject takes use.
~C. Effective independent learner use resources deliberately.#The singular subject and verb do not agree.
~D. Effective independent learners using resources deliberately.#This is a fragment.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q23::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which vocabulary choice is most precise for "ask focused questions"? {
~A. Ask random questions#This changes the meaning.
=B. Ask specific, purposeful questions#Correct. This preserves focused.
~C. Ask no questions#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Ask decorative questions#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q24::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: In college and workplace settings, this habit matters because people are expected to improve work from evidence, feedback, and reflection. Why does the author include college and workplace settings? {
~A. To say independent learning ends after high school#This contradicts the passage.
=B. To show the practical importance of improving from evidence and feedback#Correct. This explains the readiness connection.
~C. To suggest feedback is only useful at work#This is too narrow.
~D. To change the topic away from learning#This is not the function.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_UA_Q25::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: Independent learning does not mean working without support. Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which response best demonstrates Unit 1 synthesis? {
=A. Independent learning means using support responsibly: learners ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise based on evidence.#Correct. This combines paraphrase, vocabulary, and coherent explanation.
~B. Independent learning means no one helps you.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. Feedback is a word in the passage, and revision is also a word.#This identifies words but does not synthesize.
~D. Students should work alone because support is not independent.#This contradicts the passage.
}
